---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Termail — a terminal email client';
const description =
  'Termail is a terminal email client: IMAP sync, local SQLite storage, SMTP sending, keyboard-first navigation, FTS5 search, and optional AI assistance.';
const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/arjunmaybe/Termail';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="wrap" id="top">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Terminal email client</p>
          <h1 id="hero-heading">Email that stays in the terminal.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Termail syncs mail over IMAP, keeps a local SQLite copy you can
            search offline, and sends over SMTP — all through a keyboard-first
            interface built with Bun, TypeScript, and OpenTUI.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href={repoUrl} rel="noopener">View source</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="#setup">Installation instructions</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-meta">Bun v1.4.1 · IMAP + SMTP · SQLite + FTS5 · AI off by default</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="shot">
          <div class="shot-bar" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <span>termail — inbox</span>
          </div>
          <img
            src="/termail.png"
            alt="Termail terminal inbox with folders on the left and a message list on the right, using synthetic demo data"
            width="2160"
            height="736"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>Real interface, synthetic demo data — no private mail shown.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
      <h2 id="experience-heading">The product experience</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        One screen, three regions: folders on the left, messages in the
        middle, and a status bar along the bottom. Everything is reachable
        without leaving the keyboard.
      </p>
      <div class="two-col">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Inbox and folders</h3>
          <p>
            Termail discovers your account's folders on first sync, prefers
            INBOX, and tracks a per-folder checkpoint so later syncs resume
            where they left off. Move between folders with <kbd>h</kbd> /
            <kbd>Left</kbd> or <kbd>l</kbd> / <kbd>Right</kbd> (or
            <kbd>Tab</kbd>); the status bar always shows the
            current folder, message counts, and sync state.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Reading and search</h3>
          <p>
            Step through mail with <kbd>j</kbd> / <kbd>Down</kbd> and
            <kbd>k</kbd> / <kbd>Up</kbd>, open with
            <kbd>Enter</kbd>, step back with <kbd>Esc</kbd>. Press
            <kbd>/</kbd> to search the local full-text index — backed by
            SQLite FTS5 — with structured operators:
          </p>
          <p>
            <code>from:</code>, <code>to:</code>, <code>subject:</code>,
            <code>is:read</code>, <code>is:unread</code>,
            <code>has:attachment</code>, <code>folder:</code>,
            <code>after:</code>, <code>before:</code>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <table class="keys">
        <caption>Keyboard map — matches the default set in the README</caption>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>j</kbd> / <kbd>Down</kbd>, <kbd>k</kbd> / <kbd>Up</kbd></th><td>Next / previous email</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>h</kbd> / <kbd>Left</kbd>, <kbd>l</kbd> / <kbd>Right</kbd>, <kbd>Tab</kbd></th><td>Previous / next folder</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>Enter</kbd></th><td>Open the highlighted email</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>Esc</kbd></th><td>Back to the list, keeping the highlight</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>/</kbd></th><td>Search (<kbd>Esc</kbd> cancels, <kbd>Enter</kbd> submits)</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>r</kbd></th><td>Sync the current folder</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>s</kbd> / <kbd>d</kbd></th><td>AI summary / AI-drafted reply (opt-in, never auto-sends)</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><kbd>q</kbd></th><td>Quit</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="capabilities" aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading">
      <h2 id="capabilities-heading">Capabilities</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        What Termail does today — email, synchronization, configuration, and
        optional AI — as implemented in the repository.
      </p>
      <div class="two-col">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Email over IMAP and SMTP</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>IMAP sync (via imapflow) with local SQLite persistence.</li>
            <li>SMTP sending over implicit TLS or STARTTLS with password auth; no external SMTP library.</li>
            <li>SMTP needs <code>smtpHost</code> on the account; port and mode default to implicit TLS on 465.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Local-first storage and config</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Messages stored locally in SQLite with an FTS5 search index.</li>
            <li>JSON config at <code>~/.config/termail/config.json</code>, validated with Zod.</li>
            <li>UI preferences: theme, pane ratio, status bar, folder icons, compact mode.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Optional AI assistance</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Summarize the selected email (<kbd>s</kbd>) or draft a reply (<kbd>d</kbd>) via OpenRouter.</li>
            <li>Disabled by default; only runs when explicitly invoked.</li>
            <li>Drafts land in compose for review — nothing is ever auto-sent.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Built for review</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Strict TypeScript, Zod-validated config, Biome lint and format.</li>
            <li>Deterministic Bun test gate (<code>bun run test:sequential</code>).</li>
            <li>Source, docs, and security policy live in the same repository.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="limit-note">
        Current limitation: sending works through the compose service and
        AI-drafted replies routed into compose for review. There is no
        full-screen compose editor yet; external-editor composition is planned.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="setup" aria-labelledby="setup-heading">
      <h2 id="setup-heading">Getting started</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        From the repository README. Requires Bun v1.4.1 (pinned in
        <code>package.json</code> and CI).
      </p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          Clone and install:
          <div class="command">
            <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/arjunmaybe/Termail.git&#10;cd Termail&#10;bun install</code></pre>
            <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="git clone https://github.com/arjunmaybe/Termail.git
cd Termail
bun install">Copy</button>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          Run, build, and check:
          <div class="command">
            <pre><code>bun run dev&#10;bun run build&#10;bun run test:sequential&#10;bun run typecheck&#10;bun run lint</code></pre>
            <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="bun run dev
bun run build
bun run test:sequential
bun run typecheck
bun run lint">Copy</button>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          Add accounts to <code>~/.config/termail/config.json</code>, then save
          the password once into the OS credential store (input is hidden):
          <div class="command">
            <pre><code>bun run src/main.ts --set-password work</code></pre>
            <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="bun run src/main.ts --set-password work">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <p>
            Also available: <code>--set-oauth-token</code>,
            <code>--delete-password</code>,
            <code>--delete-oauth-token</code>. On platforms without OS
            credential storage, use per-account environment variables instead
            (see Security).
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="security" aria-labelledby="security-heading">
      <h2 id="security-heading">Security and privacy</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        A plain summary of the implementation and <a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`} rel="noopener">security policy</a> —
        what stays local, what leaves the machine, and what Termail does not promise.
      </p>
      <div class="two-col">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Local mail storage</h3>
          <p>
            Mail is stored in a local SQLite database that is
            <strong>not encrypted by Termail</strong>. On POSIX systems
            Termail restricts its data directories to owner-only access; on
            Windows no ACL hardening is performed, so configure filesystem
            ACLs externally on shared machines.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Credentials</h3>
          <p>
            Passwords and tokens never live in <code>config.json</code>, the
            mail database, logs, or issue reports. The fastest option is the
            one-time OS credential-store save (Windows Credential Manager).
            OS storage is implemented on Windows only; elsewhere — and for
            headless use — set
            <code>TERMAIL_&lt;ACCOUNT_ID&gt;_PASSWORD</code> or
            <code>TERMAIL_&lt;ACCOUNT_ID&gt;_OAUTH_TOKEN</code>. Environment
            variables take precedence when both are configured.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>What the AI provider receives</h3>
          <p>
            Only when you press <kbd>s</kbd> or <kbd>d</kbd>: the selected
            email's headers (From, To, Cc, Subject, Date) and up to
            <code>maxBodyChars</code> body characters (default 8000, sent
            inside an explicit <code>&lt;email&gt;</code> block marked as
            data). The default endpoint is OpenRouter's chat-completions API.
            Output is display text or a draft for review.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Reporting</h3>
          <p>
            Only the latest <code>main</code> commit receives security fixes.
            Report issues through GitHub private vulnerability reporting with
            redacted material — never live credentials or mailbox contents.
            There is no paid bounty program.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What do I need to run Termail?</summary>
          <p>Bun v1.4.1, a clone of the repository, and <code>bun install</code>. You also need at least one email account with IMAP details (and <code>smtpHost</code> if you want to send).</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where does my configuration live?</summary>
          <p>At <code>~/.config/termail/config.json</code> (version 1), validated with Zod. It holds database path, UI preferences, accounts, and AI settings — never secrets.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How are passwords handled on Linux or macOS?</summary>
          <p>OS credential storage is Windows-only today. On other platforms, set per-account secrets in the environment: <code>TERMAIL_&lt;ACCOUNT_ID&gt;_PASSWORD</code> or <code>TERMAIL_&lt;ACCOUNT_ID&gt;_OAUTH_TOKEN</code>.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is my local mail database encrypted?</summary>
          <p>No. Termail does not encrypt the SQLite database. POSIX systems get owner-only directories and files; Windows needs externally configured filesystem ACLs on shared machines.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does the AI act on my mailbox?</summary>
          <p>No. AI only summarizes or drafts when you explicitly press <kbd>s</kbd> or <kbd>d</kbd>. Drafts go into compose for review and nothing is auto-sent. AI is off by default.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I compose and send a new message today?</summary>
          <p>Sending works through the compose service and AI-drafted replies routed into compose for review. There is no full-screen compose editor yet.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const text = button.getAttribute('data-copy') ?? '';
        const label = button.textContent;
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
          button.textContent = 'Copied';
        } catch {
          button.textContent = 'Select manually';
        }
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = label;
        }, 1600);
      });
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
